\subsection{Three corollaries}\label{sec:four-corollaries}
We apply the exact equality between the rational zero projection of
$P_*$ and ordinary $\Z$ proved in Theorem~\ref{thm:target}.

\begin{lemma}[Exact seven-variable pole statement]\label{hyp:o8-pole}
If $b\ne0$ and $\Psi(b)$, then $v_p(b)$ is not a negative odd integer
for every $p\notin\{2,3,17\}$. Conversely, $\Psi(b)$ holds whenever
$b>0$, the denominator of $b$ in lowest terms is a square, and $b$ is
a square in each of $\Q_2,\Q_3,\Q_{17}$.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
These are Lemmas~\ref{lem:original-seven-parity-soundness} and
\ref{lem:original-seven-parity-completeness}. Their proof gives the
simultaneous two-twist construction explicitly, and applies the existing
Theorem~\ref{hyp:RC} and Lemma~\ref{lem:corank}. It introduces no new
simultaneous-realization assumption.
\end{proof}

\begin{lemma}[The exact one-sided assertion]
\label{lem:original-seven-parity-soundness}
If $b\ne0$ and $\Psi(b)$, then $v_\ell(b)$ is not a negative odd
integer for any prime $\ell\notin\{2,3,17\}$.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}
Suppose $k=v_\ell(b)<0$ is odd. Equation~\eqref{eq:seven-param}
forces $1+bt^2\ne0$: if it vanished, its right side would be $2b\ne0$.
If $t=0$, then $U=b$. Otherwise $v_\ell(bt^2)$ is odd and nonzero,
so $(1-bt^2)/(1+bt^2)$ is a unit. Thus $v_\ell(U)=k$ in all cases,
and $v_\ell(B-U^2)=2k$.

Finally fix the integers
\begin{equation}\label{eq:v5-fixed-constant}
 C=3^{2^{26}},\qquad \mathsf S=C^2=3^{2^{27}},\qquad
 \kappa=\mathsf S^2=3^{2^{28}}.
\end{equation}
The symbol \texttt{S} in the coefficient files means $\mathsf S$;
it is not the point $S$ and is not a quantified coordinate.
Write $f(S)=f_0+f_1\sqrt2$, retain three private rational witnesses
$u,v,w$, and impose
\begin{equation}\label{eq:v5-physical-anchor}
 u^2+6v^2-2w^2-3(f_0^2+f_0f_1-f_1^2)^2+2\mathsf S^2=0.
\end{equation}
This completes the rational source. Every rational expression has the
displayed guard or a domain implication already proved. Equations
\eqref{eq:v5-zero-pole} and \eqref{eq:v5-scalar-pole} retain their
degenerate witness values.
